{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-38484","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65085","text":"TRAAVIIS — Split Evaluation Closure ("},{"id":"spn-65086","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-65087","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-38485","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65088","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date"},{"id":"spn-65089","text":" 2026-07-24 · "},{"id":"spn-65090","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status"},{"id":"spn-65091","text":" shipped, 15 new laws green, 314 tests green "},{"id":"spn-65092","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope"},{"id":"spn-65093","text":" RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md §7 — the last unbuilt item in the build order that is not explicitly deferred. "},{"id":"spn-65094","marks":["code"],"text":"serve"},{"id":"spn-65095","text":" (D5) and "},{"id":"spn-65096","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-65097","text":" remain open."}]},{"id":"blk-38486","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65098","text":"1. What shipped"}]},{"id":"blk-38487","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65099","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-65100","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-65101","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-65102","text":" closed authoring. "},{"id":"spn-65103","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-65104","text":" closed one task. The remaining gap was the one §7 names last:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38489","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65105","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-65106","text":" — run an agent over a split, emit an "},{"id":"spn-65107","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-65108","text":" per task, score."}]}],"id":"blk-38488","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-38490","kind":"code","language":"sh","text":"trvs pack lab lab-pkg\ntrvs eval lab-pkg --split test --output episodes/ --agent python3 agent.py\ntrvs verify-episode episodes/episode-cfef6da4…      # replays with no agent"},{"id":"blk-38491","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65109","text":"Verified end to end on a hand-authored three-task environment:"}]},{"id":"blk-38492","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"pack →  env-aa7df5dd…   task-3b4b2599…  task-082e11c1…  task-0cd4992e…\n        closure ✓  reopened ✓\n\neval --split test\n  [1/2] ✓ task-082e11c181f3be21aa82e138  ok  reward 1\n  [2/2] ✓ task-0cd4992e274e07fc7da0bddd  ok  reward 1\n  ok            2/2\n  mean reward   1\n  evaluation    episodes/evaluation.json\n\nverify-episode (each, no agent process) → ✓ closed"},{"id":"blk-38493","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65110","text":"2. The load-bearing decision: "},{"id":"spn-65111","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-65112","text":" mints no identity"}]},{"id":"blk-38494","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65113","text":"§1's ladder ends at "},{"id":"spn-65114","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-65115","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-65116","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-65117","text":". There is "},{"id":"spn-65118","marks":["bold"],"text":"no rung for \"a run over a split\""},{"id":"spn-65119","text":", so this command does not create one. What it returns is an "},{"id":"spn-65120","marks":["italic"],"text":"index"},{"id":"spn-65121","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-38495","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"evaluation_version\": \"traaviis.evaluation.v1\",\n  \"env_id\": \"env-…\", \"split\": \"test\",\n  \"episodes\": [ {\"task_id\": \"task-…\", \"episode_id\": \"episode-…\",\n                 \"status\": \"ok\", \"reward\": 1.0, \"bundle\": \"episode-…\"} ],\n  \"totals\": {\"tasks\": 2, \"ok\": 2, \"reward_mean\": 1.0, …} }"},{"id":"blk-38496","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65122","text":"Every id in it is derived somewhere else. The index itself is not content-addressed and carries no id — a law (E5) scans the emitted JSON and fails on any "},{"id":"spn-65123","marks":["code"],"text":"<prefix>-<hex>"},{"id":"spn-65124","text":" family outside "},{"id":"spn-65125","marks":["code"],"text":"{env, task, episode, snap, sem}"},{"id":"spn-65126","text":", and on any "},{"id":"spn-65127","marks":["code"],"text":"evaluation_id"},{"id":"spn-65128","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-65129","marks":["code"],"text":"run_id"},{"id":"spn-65130","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-65131","marks":["code"],"text":"eval_id"},{"id":"spn-65132","text":" key."}]},{"id":"blk-38497","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65133","text":"This is deliberate restraint, not an oversight. A defensible "},{"id":"spn-65134","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-…"},{"id":"spn-65135","text":" would have to close over "},{"id":"spn-65136","marks":["italic"],"text":"the agent"},{"id":"spn-65137","text":", and there is no agent identity rung — so any id minted today would be under-determined, and a later real one would silently disagree with it. See §6.1."}]},{"id":"blk-38498","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65138","text":"3. Nothing runs until everything checkable has been checked"}]},{"id":"blk-38499","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65139","text":"The order mirrors "},{"id":"spn-65140","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-65141","text":"'s, for the same reason:"}]},{"id":"blk-38500","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"1. open_package     reopen through §5a — env-/task-/rew-/snap- ALL re-derived\n                    from the written bytes\n2. resolve split    the split exists, is non-empty, every member is in-closure\n3. admit subject    bind the on-disk tree to snapshot.json (once, shared)\n--- only now is a process launched ---\n4. per task         evaluate → optionally persist episode-<id>/\n5. aggregate        index written atomically (temp sibling + one rename)"},{"id":"blk-38501","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65142","text":"Two laws prove the boundary is real rather than decorative: E2 tampers a packed task and E2b drifts one subject byte, then passes an agent that writes a marker file. Both refuse with a typed code ("},{"id":"spn-65143","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_TASK_ID"},{"id":"spn-65144","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-65145","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBJECT_*"},{"id":"spn-65146","text":") "},{"id":"spn-65147","marks":["bold"],"text":"and the marker never appears"},{"id":"spn-65148","text":" — a broken package costs zero episodes, not N wasted ones."}]},{"id":"blk-38502","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65149","text":"4. A split is a set — so its order is not observable"}]},{"id":"blk-38503","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65150","text":"§3 says splits are \""},{"id":"spn-65151","marks":["bold"],"text":"named sets"},{"id":"spn-65152","text":" of "},{"id":"spn-65153","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-65154","text":" ids\". Taken literally that has a consequence the previous "},{"id":"spn-65155","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-65156","text":" did not honour: it stored split membership in source order, so listing the same two tasks the other way round produced a different "},{"id":"spn-65157","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-65158","text":". Two identical environments, two identities."}]},{"id":"blk-38504","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65159","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-65160","text":" now canonicalizes a split as a "},{"id":"spn-65161","marks":["bold"],"text":"sorted set"},{"id":"spn-65162","text":", and a repeated member is "},{"id":"spn-65163","marks":["code"],"text":"SPLIT_DUPLICATE"},{"id":"spn-65164","text":" rather than being silently collapsed (pack never repairs a scaffold). "},{"id":"spn-65165","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-65166","text":" then derives its run order as the sorted task ids, so the order tasks execute in is a function of the environment, never of how someone typed the manifest. E1 packs two environments differing only in split order and asserts byte-identical "},{"id":"spn-65167","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-65168","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-38505","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65169","text":"5. Laws (15 new, all green)"}]},{"id":"blk-38506","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65170","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_eval_split.py"},{"id":"spn-65171","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-38507","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38509","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65172","marks":["bold"],"text":"E1"},{"id":"spn-65173","text":" split order does not move "},{"id":"spn-65174","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-65175","text":"; the packed manifest is sorted ·"}]}],"id":"blk-38508","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-38510","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65176","text":"duplicate member refused, nothing written."}]},{"id":"blk-38511","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38513","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65177","marks":["bold"],"text":"E2"},{"id":"spn-65178","text":" tampered package and drifted subject both refuse **before any agent"}]}],"id":"blk-38512","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-38514","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65179","text":"process starts** (proved with a marker-writing agent)."}]},{"id":"blk-38515","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38517","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65180","marks":["bold"],"text":"E3"},{"id":"spn-65181","text":" unknown / empty / foreign-member splits are typed refusals, and the"}]}],"id":"blk-38516","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-38518","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65182","text":"unknown-split error names the splits that do exist."}]},{"id":"blk-38519","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38521","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65183","marks":["bold"],"text":"E4"},{"id":"spn-65184","text":" run order is the sorted task ids regardless of manifest order."}]}],"id":"blk-38520","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38523","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65185","marks":["bold"],"text":"E5"},{"id":"spn-65186","text":" the index invents no identity (id-family scan + forbidden keys)."}]}],"id":"blk-38522","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38525","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65187","marks":["bold"],"text":"E6/E10"},{"id":"spn-65188","text":" one episode per task, distinct ids for distinct tasks, totals are"}]}],"id":"blk-38524","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-38526","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65189","text":"real arithmetic over the episodes."}]},{"id":"blk-38527","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38529","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65190","marks":["bold"],"text":"E8"},{"id":"spn-65191","text":" persisted episodes are genuine closed bundles — each re-verified with"}]}],"id":"blk-38528","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-38530","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65192","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs verify-episode"},{"id":"spn-65193","text":", no agent — and the index round-trips."}]},{"id":"blk-38531","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38533","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65194","marks":["bold"],"text":"E9"},{"id":"spn-65195","text":" a bad task is recorded and the split continues (2 of 3 still score 1)."}]}],"id":"blk-38532","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38535","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65196","marks":["bold"],"text":"E11"},{"id":"spn-65197","text":" a "},{"id":"spn-65198","marks":["code"],"text":"trvm.world.v1"},{"id":"spn-65199","text":" package is refused "},{"id":"spn-65200","marks":["italic"],"text":"by name"}]}],"id":"blk-38534","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-38536","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65201","text":"("},{"id":"spn-65202","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBSTRATE_NOT_EVALUABLE"},{"id":"spn-65203","text":"), not half-run."}]},{"id":"blk-38537","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38539","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65204","marks":["bold"],"text":"E13"},{"id":"spn-65205","text":" two runs of one split agree exactly ("},{"id":"spn-65206","marks":["code"],"text":"a == b"},{"id":"spn-65207","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-38538","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38541","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65208","text":"CLI: exit 0 all-ok · exit 1 ran-and-disagreed ("},{"id":"spn-65209","marks":["code"],"text":"ok 2/3"},{"id":"spn-65210","text":") · exit 2 unknown"}]}],"id":"blk-38540","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-38542","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65211","text":"split / missing package · "},{"id":"spn-65212","marks":["code"],"text":"--json"},{"id":"spn-65213","text":" emits the index."}]},{"id":"blk-38543","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65214","text":"Regression: "},{"id":"spn-65215","marks":["bold"],"text":"314 tests green, 0 failures, 0 skips"},{"id":"spn-65216","text":" — admission 16, cli_evalone 18, cli 12, episode_evidence 56, evalone 14, "},{"id":"spn-65217","marks":["bold"],"text":"eval_split 15"},{"id":"spn-65218","text":", execfacts 8, forge_adapter 6, identity 25, pack 18, patchapply 10, paths 10, real_residency 9, reward 17, runner 10, scaffold 16, snapshot 10, substrate_verifiers 24, vcontext 5, verifiers 15."}]},{"id":"blk-38544","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65219","text":"6. Autonomous decisions — flagged for GPT-5.6"}]},{"id":"blk-38545","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38547","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65220","marks":["bold"],"text":"`eval` mints no artifact id."},{"id":"spn-65221","text":" The index is "},{"id":"spn-65222","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.evaluation.v1"},{"id":"spn-65223","text":" and is"}]}],"id":"blk-38546","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-38548","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65224","text":"not content-addressed. If you want a run over a split to "},{"id":"spn-65225","marks":["italic"],"text":"be"},{"id":"spn-65226","text":" an artifact, it needs an agent identity rung first — otherwise the id closes over less than the thing it names. I did not invent either. "},{"id":"spn-65227","marks":["bold"],"text":"Confirm, or rule the agent rung."}]},{"id":"blk-38549","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38551","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65228","marks":["bold"],"text":"Splits are canonicalized as sorted sets, and this changes `env-…`"},{"id":"spn-65229","text":" for any"}]}],"id":"blk-38550","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-38552","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65230","text":"environment whose split members were not already in sorted order. It is the literal reading of §3 (\"named sets\"), and it makes reordering non-identity — but it "},{"id":"spn-65231","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-65232","text":" a behaviour change to a shipped command. Confirm."}]},{"id":"blk-38553","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38555","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65233","marks":["bold"],"text":"`SPLIT_DUPLICATE` refuses rather than collapses"},{"id":"spn-65234","text":" a repeated member,"}]}],"id":"blk-38554","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-38556","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65235","text":"matching the "},{"id":"spn-65236","marks":["code"],"text":"RemoveObject"},{"id":"spn-65237","text":"/no-auto-repair discipline."}]},{"id":"blk-38557","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38559","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65238","marks":["bold"],"text":"Verifier wiring moved out of the CLI"},{"id":"spn-65239","text":" into "},{"id":"spn-65240","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/wiring.py"},{"id":"spn-65241","text":". It was"}]}],"id":"blk-38558","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-38560","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65242","text":"CLI-private, so a library caller got "},{"id":"spn-65243","marks":["italic"],"text":"zero"},{"id":"spn-65244","text":" verifiers and every episode came back invalid-config. A task's verifier set must be a function of the task, not of the caller, or two runs of one task are not comparable. This was a real defect found by the E6 law, not a refactor for taste."}]},{"id":"blk-38561","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38563","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65245","marks":["bold"],"text":"A low reward is not a disagreement."},{"id":"spn-65246","text":" Exit 1 fires only on "},{"id":"spn-65247","marks":["code"],"text":"invalid"},{"id":"spn-65248","text":" /"}]}],"id":"blk-38562","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-38564","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65249","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-65250","text":" episodes; an agent that legitimately scores 0.25 exits 0. "},{"id":"spn-65251","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-65252","text":" scores, it does not judge."}]},{"id":"blk-38565","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38567","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65253","marks":["bold"],"text":"One subject per environment"},{"id":"spn-65254","text":", admitted once and shared by every task in"}]}],"id":"blk-38566","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":6},{"id":"blk-38568","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65255","text":"the split. That is the shape "},{"id":"spn-65256","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-65257","text":" emits today. Per-task subjects would need a different manifest, not a different runner."}]},{"id":"blk-38569","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-38571","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65258","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trvm.world.v1` is refused by name."},{"id":"spn-65259","text":" It packs and reopens fine, but the"}]}],"id":"blk-38570","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":7},{"id":"blk-38572","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65260","text":"Episode Kernel over a world subject (D5) is unbuilt, so it is a typed refusal rather than a partial run."}]},{"id":"blk-38573","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-65261","text":"7. Not built"}]},{"id":"blk-38574","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65262","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs serve --ors/--mcp"},{"id":"spn-65263","text":" (needs the D5 process model), "},{"id":"spn-65264","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-65265","text":" (the outer content-addressed package from D3), and the REPL. With "},{"id":"spn-65266","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-65267","text":" shipped, "},{"id":"spn-65268","marks":["bold"],"text":"§7's build order is exhausted"},{"id":"spn-65269","text":" — everything remaining was explicitly deferred by ruling, so this is a natural halt point."}]},{"id":"blk-38575","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-65270","text":"MIT licensed · TRAAVIIS Holdings · part of the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraknvvf6y6oagficg7oejbviv7tbubogmhmzuaqubb7vexiijobtkq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}